{#
    The Terms PDF of one Terms version, in one locale. It holds no order data, so one PDF serves every order that
    accepted the version.

    Variables:
    - version: the TermsVersionInterface
    - translation: the version's TermsVersionTranslationInterface in the locale
    - locale_code: the locale the PDF is in. The request's locale isn't used, so pass this one to every trans and format_date
    - channel: the ChannelInterface. Relative URLs are made absolute against its hostname after this template renders

    Images are downloaded and inlined after this template renders, so the PDF engine never fetches anything. dompdf
    bundles DejaVu Sans, which covers far more characters than its core fonts.

    The PDFs are cached. After overriding this template, clear the cache: bin/console cache:pool:clear setono_sylius_terms.pdf
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ locale_code|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>{{ translation.name }}</title>
    <style>
        @page {
            size: A4;
            margin: 2cm;
        }

        body {
            font-family: "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
            font-size: 10pt;
            line-height: 1.4;
            color: #222;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 18pt;
            margin: 0 0 4pt;
        }

        .version {
            color: #555;
            margin: 0 0 18pt;
        }

        table {
            border-collapse: collapse;
            width: 100%;
        }

        th, td {
            border: 1px solid #999;
            padding: 4pt;
            text-align: left;
            vertical-align: top;
        }

        img {
            max-width: 100%;
        }

        /* The # permalinks that the content renderer puts after each ## heading for the Terms page */
        a[title="Permalink"] {
            display: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>{{ translation.name }}</h1>

    <p class="version">
        {{- 'setono_sylius_terms.pdf.version_line'|trans({
            '%number%': version.number,
            '%date%': version.inForceFrom|format_date('long', locale: locale_code),
        }, 'messages', locale_code) -}}
    </p>

    {{ translation.content|terms_content }}
</body>
</html>
